<title>BELGIUM: Rise in Belgian jobless rate seasonal - minister.</title>
<headline>Rise in Belgian jobless rate seasonal - minister.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A rise in the Belgian jobless rate to 13.7 percent in July from 12.6 percent in June was mainly seasonal, Labour Minister Miet Smet said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;It is mainly due to the slowdown in economic activity in the summer holiday period, indemnities paid to youths ending internships, and the re-registration of contract staff in the educational sector,&quot; the minister said.</p>
<p>In July 1996 the unemployment rate rose to 14.0 percent from 12.8 percent in June 1996.</p>
